  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>Teoman Lam, Zurich, Switzerland.<br />Contact: via <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/teomanlam" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.</p>

  <h2>2. Scope</h2>
  <p>This policy covers the website teolam.com. It applies under the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP/nDSG) and, where visitors are in the EU/EEA, the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).</p>

  <h2>3. Hosting and delivery (Cloudflare)</h2>
  <p>This website is hosted and delivered by Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. When you visit the site, Cloudflare processes technical data that your browser sends automatically: IP address, date and time, requested page, referrer, browser and operating system. This is necessary to deliver the website and protect it against attacks. Cloudflare keeps this data only briefly.</p>
  <p>Legal basis: overriding legitimate interest in a secure, working website (Art. 31 FADP; Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</p>

  <h2>4. Analytics (Cloudflare Web Analytics)</h2>
  <p>To understand how many people visit the site, it uses Cloudflare Web Analytics. It sets no cookies, does not use local storage and does not fingerprint visitors. It records anonymous, aggregated information: the page visited, referrer, browser type, device type and country. No profiles of individual visitors are created.</p>
  <p>Legal basis: legitimate interest in understanding the reach of the website (Art. 31 FADP; Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</p>

  <h2>5. Transfers outside Switzerland and the EU</h2>
  <p>Cloudflare may process data in the USA and other countries. Cloudflare is certified under the EU-US and Swiss-US Data Privacy Frameworks and also uses Standard Contractual Clauses.</p>

  <h2>6. Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>This website sets no cookies. If you use the light/dark mode switch, your choice is saved in your browser's local storage (key <code>theme</code>) so the site remembers it. It never leaves your device and you can delete it at any time in your browser settings.</p>

  <h2>7. External links</h2>
  <p>Links to LinkedIn and the Project Management Institute (PMI) open external websites. Only when you click them do those providers receive data, under their own privacy policies.</p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to access, rectify and delete your personal data, to restrict or object to processing, and to data portability. To exercise these rights, contact me via LinkedIn. You may also lodge a complaint with the Swiss Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner (FDPIC) or, in the EU, with your local data protection authority.</p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>This policy may be updated when the website changes. The current version is always published on this page.</p>
</LegalPage>
